searchers\nResearchers\nInstructors\nStaff\nProspective continuing education students\nAlumni\nJournalists\nRefugees (in German only)\nClose\nLanguage\nEnglish\nDeutsch\n/en/sitemap.json\nMIN Doctoral Gateway\nResearch\nBiology\nChemistry\nEarth Sciences\nInformatics\nMathematics\nPhysics\nDoctorate at MIN\nFirst steps\nTypes of doctorate\nRequirements\nAdmission\nEnrollment\nDuration\nDoctoral exams\nDownloads\nFinancing\nEmployment\nScholarships\nMobility grants\nAwards\nSkill development\nGeventis\nLanguage courses\nGood scientific practice\nCareer Development Cycle\nHamburg Research Academy\nCareer Center\nHUL\nPIASTA\nAfter Doctorate\nProfessional development\nAcademic career\nEntrepreneurship & startups\nScience management\nJob fairs and websites\nService\nFAQ for doctoral studies\nMIN Graduate Center (MINGZ)\nMINGZ Newsletter\nMINGZ Blog\nNew to Hamburg / International Doctorate\nEqual opportunities\nProject ProBe / IDP\nCounseling\nContact\nPhoto: UHH/shell\nMIN doctoral gateway\nUHH\nDoctoral Studies\nMIN Doctoral Gateway\nFinancing\nEmployment\nEmployment\nDoctoral researchers may finance their studies through employment at the university (internal funding) or through project-specific external funding. Doctoral supervisors can only award job contracts if they are available. One is awarded salary grade E13 according to the German collective wage agreement (TV\u00f6D). The employment contracts can cover 50-100% of the full working time and are based on TV\u00f6D 13 (approx. 1.800 \u20ac before tax at 50% employment). For jobs financed through state funds, the teaching obligation is regulated in the employment contract (2 SWS per semester at 50% employment); for jobs financed by third-party funds, however, there is normally no contractual teaching obligation.\nFor details on the current job opportunities at Universit\u00e4t Hamburg, please see the website of your respective department and the university homepage. You can also check the websites of the graduate schools for vacant positions.\nYou also have the opportunity to complete your doctoral studies at one of the following external research institutions in cooperation with Universit\u00e4t Hamburg:\nHelmholtz Association (German Research Centres)\nDeutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron (DESY)\nHelmholtz-Zentrum Geesthacht, Centre for Materials and Coastal Research (HZG)\nMax Planck Society\nMax Planck Institute for the Structure and Dynamics of Matter (MPSD)\nMax Planck Institute for Meteorology (MPI-M)\nLeibniz Association\nHeinrich Pette Institute (HPI)\nBernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine (BNITM)\nUniversity Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf (UKE)\nInformation on work contracts and job opportunities can mostly be found on the institutional websites.\nFinancing\nEmployment\nScholarships\nMobility grants\nAwards\nDr. Anne-Catherin Zappe\nAdvisor for Internationalization and Support for Doctoral and Early Career Researchers\nFaculty of Mathematics, Informatics and Natural Sciences\nWelckerstra\u00dfe 8\n20354 Hamburg\nTel: +49 40 42838-9076\nFax: +49 40 42838-7437\nEmail: mingz\"AT\"uni-hamburg.de\nLast update: 7 April 2021\nFeedback\nLegal notice\nPrivacy statement\nAccessibility\nSite map\nUniversity of Hamburg\nInnovating and Cooperating for a Sustainable Future in a Digital Age\nStudies\nProspective students\nContinuing education\nResearch\nTeaching at UHH\nDoctoral studies\nJob opportunities\nKnowledge exchange\nUniversity\nExcellence\nFaculties\nAlumni\nContact\nCampus Navigator\nUHHApp\nEmergencies, safety and security\nAntidiscrimination\n\u00a9 2026 University of Hamburg. All rights reserved", "links": [["Zur Metanavigation", "https://www.promovieren.uni-hamburg.de/en/min/finanzierung/anstellung-und-arbeitsvertraege.html#meta"], ["Zur Hauptnavigation", "https://www.promovieren.uni-hamburg.de/en/min/finanzierung/anstellung-und-arbeitsvertraege.html#nav"], ["Zur Suche", "https://www.promovieren.uni-hamburg.de/en/min/finanzierung/anstellung-und-arbeitsvert